<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Southern Copper sale seen about A$20 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Southern Copper sale seen about A$20 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Market sources on Thursday valued the sale by RTZ Corp Plc-CRA Ltd's of assets of Southern Copper Ltd at around A$20 million.</p>
<p>RTZ-CRA said on Wednesday it had disposed of the land, buildings, plant and equipment owned by Southern Copper to the Port Kembla Copper group of companies.</p>
<p>The value of these net assets represented less than one percent of the net assets of the RTZ-CRA Group, RTZ-CRA said.</p>
<p>The complex has been on care and maintenance since early 1995.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
